the `**generation_kwargs` argument when you initialize\n    42\u2192    the component or when you run it. Any parameter that works with\n    43\u2192    `openai.ChatCompletion.create` will work here too.\n    44\u2192\n    45\u2192    For details on OpenAI API parameters, see\n    46\u2192    [OpenAI documentation](https://platform.openai.com/docs/api-reference/chat).\n    47\u2192\n    48\u2192    ### Usage example\n    49\u2192\n    50\u2192    ```python\n    51\u2192    from haystack.components.generators.chat import OpenAIChatGenerator\n    52\u2192    from haystack.dataclasses import ChatMessage\n    53\u2192\n    54\u2192    messages = [ChatMessage.from_user(\"What's Natural Language Processing?\")]\n    55\u2192\n    56\u2192    client = OpenAIChatGenerator()\n    57\u2192    response = client.run(messages)\n    58\u2192    print(response)\n    59\u2192    ```\n    60\u2192    Output:\n    61\u2192    ```\n    62\u2192    {'replies':\n    63\u2192        [ChatMessage(content='Natural Language Processing (NLP) is a branch of artificial intelligence\n    64\u2192            that focuses on enabling computers to understand, interpret, and generate human language in\n    65\u2192            a way that is meaningful and useful.',\n    66\u2192         role=<ChatRole.ASSISTANT: 'assistant'>, name=None,\n    67\u2192         meta={'model': 'gpt-4o-mini', 'index': 0, 'finish_reason': 'stop',\n    68\u2192         'usage': {'prompt_tokens': 15, 'completion_tokens': 36, 'total_tokens': 51}})\n    69\u2192        ]\n    70\u2192    }\n    71\u2192    ```\n    72\u2192    \"\"\"\n    73\u2192\n    74\u2192    def __init__(  # pylint: disable=too-many-positional-arguments\n    75\u2192        self,\n    76\u2192        api_key: Secret = Secret.from_env_var(\"OPENAI_API_KEY\"),\n    77\u2192        model: str = \"gpt-4o-mini\",\n    78\u2192        streaming_callback: Optional[StreamingCallbackT] = None,\n    79\u2192        api_base_url: Optional[str] = None,\n    80\u2192        organization: Optional[str] = None,\n    81\u2192        generation_kwargs: Optional[Dict[str, Any]] = None,\n    82\u2192        timeout: Optional[float] = None,\n    83\u2192        max_retries: Optional[int] = None,\n    84\u2192        tools: Optional[List[Tool]] = None,\n    85\u2192        tools_strict: bool = False,\n    86\u2192    ):\n    87\u2192        \"\"\"\n    88\u2192        Creates an instance of OpenAIChatGenerator. Unless specified otherwise in `model`, uses OpenAI's gpt-4o-mini\n    89\u2192\n    90\u2192        Before initializing the component, you can set the 'OPENAI_TIMEOUT' and 'OPENAI_MAX_RETRIES'\n    91\u2192        environment variables to override the `timeout` and `max_retries` parameters respectively\n    92\u2192        in the OpenAI client.\n    93\u2192\n    94\u2192        :param api_key: The OpenAI API key.\n    95\u2192            You can set it with an environment variable `OPENAI_API_KEY`, or pass with this parameter\n    96\u2192            during initialization.\n    97\u2192        :param model: The name of the model to use.\n    98\u2192        :param streaming_callback: A callback function that is called when a new token is received from the stream.\n    99\u2192            The callback function accepts [StreamingChunk](https://docs.haystack.deepset.ai/docs/data-classes#streamingchunk)\n   100\u2192            as an argument.\n   101\u2192        :param api_base_url: An optional base URL.\n   102\u2192        :param organization: Your organization ID, defaults to `None`. See\n   103\u2192        [production best practices](https://platform.openai.com/docs/guides/production-best-practices/setting-up-your-organization).\n   104\u2192        :param generation_kwargs: Other parameters to use for the model. These parameters are sent directly to\n   105\u2192            the OpenAI endpoint. See OpenAI [documentation](https://platform.openai.com/docs/api-reference/chat) for\n   106\u2192            more details.\n   107\u2192            Some of the supported parameters:\n   108\u2192            - `max_tokens`: The maximum number of tokens the output text can have.\n   109\u2192            - `temperature`: What sampling temperature to use. Higher values mean the model will take more risks.\n   110\u2192                Try 0.9 for more creative applications and 0 (argmax sampling) for ones with a well-defined answer.\n   111\u2192            - `top_p`: An alternative to sampling with temperature, called nucleus sampling, where the model\n   112\u2192                considers the results of the tokens with top_p probability mass. For example, 0.1 means only the tokens\n   113\u2192                comprising the top 10% probability mass are considered.\n   114\u2192            - `n`: How many completions to generate for each prompt. For example, if the LLM gets 3 prompts and n is 2,\n   115\u2192                it will generate two completions for each of the three prompts, ending up with 6 completions in total.\n   116\u2192            - `stop`: One or more sequences after which the LLM should stop generating tokens.\n   117\u2192            - `presence_penalty`: What penalty to apply if a token is already present at all. Bigger values mean\n   118\u2192                the model will be less likely to repeat the same token in the text.\n   119\u2192            - `frequency_penalty`: What penalty to apply if a token has already been generated in the text.\n   120\u2192                Bigger values mean the model will be less likely to repeat the same token in the text.\n   121\u2192            - `logit_bias`: Add a logit bias to specific tokens. The keys of the dictionary are tokens, and the\n   122\u2192                values are the bias to add to that token.\n   123\u2192        :param timeout:\n   124\u2192            Timeout for OpenAI client calls. If not set, it defaults to either the\n   125\u2192            `OPENAI_TIMEOUT` environment variable, or 30 seconds.\n   126\u2192        :param max_retries:\n   127\u2192            Maximum number of retries to contact OpenAI after an internal error.\n   128\u2192            If not set, it defaults to either the `OPENAI_MAX_RETRIES` environment variable, or set to 5.\n   129\u2192        :param tools:\n   130\u2192            A list of tools for which the model can prepare calls.\n   131\u2192        :param tools_strict:\n   132\u2192            Whether to enable strict schema adherence for tool calls. If set to `True`, the model will follow exactly\n   133\u2192            the schema provided in the `parameters` field of the tool definition, but this may increase latency.\n   134\u2192        \"\"\"\n   135\u2192        self.api_key = api_key\n   136\u2192        self.model = model\n   137\u2192        self.generation_kwargs = generation_kwargs or {}\n   138\u2192        self.streaming_callback = streaming_callback\n   139\u2192        self.api_base_url = api_base_url\n   140\u2192        self.organization = organization\n   141\u2192        self.timeout = timeout\n   142\u2192        self.max_retries = max_retries\n   143\u2192        self.tools = tools\n   144\u2192        self.tools_strict = tools_strict\n   145\u2192\n   146\u2192        _check_duplicate_tool_names(tools)\n   147\u2192\n   148\u2192        if timeout is None:\n   149\u2192            timeout = float(os.environ.get(\"OPENAI_TIMEOUT\", 30.0))\n   150\u2192        if max_retries is None:\n   151\u2192            max_retries = int(os.environ.get(\"OPENAI_MAX_RETRIES\", 5))\n   152\u2192\n   153\u2192        client_args: Dict[str, Any] = {\n   154\u2192            \"api_key\": api_key.resolve_value(),\n   155\u2192            \"organization\": organization,\n   156\u2192            \"base_url\": api_base_url,\n   157\u2192            \"timeout\": timeout,\n   158\u2192            \"max_retries\": max_retries,\n   159\u2192        }\n   160\u2192\n   161\u2192        self.client = OpenAI(**client_args)\n   162\u2192        self.async_client = AsyncOpenAI(**client_args)\n   163\u2192\n   164\u2192    def _get_telemetry_data(self) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n   165\u2192        \"\"\"\n   166\u2192        Data that is sent to Posthog for usage analytics.\n   167\u2192        \"\"\"\n   168\u2192        return {\"model\": self.model}\n   169\u2192\n   170\u2192    def to_dict(self) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n   171\u2192        \"\"\"\n   172\u2192        Serialize this component to a dictionary.\n   173\u2192\n   174\u2192        :returns:\n   175\u2192            The serialized component as a dictionary.\n   176\u2192        \"\"\"\n   177\u2192        callback_name = serialize_callable(self.streaming_callback) if self.streaming_callback else None\n   178\u2192        return default_to_dict(\n   179\u2192            self,\n   180\u2192            model=self.model,\n   181\u2192            streaming_callback=callback_name,\n   182\u2192            api_base_url=self.api_base_url,\n   183\u2192            organization=self.organization,\n   184\u2192            generation_kwargs=self.generation_kwargs,\n   185\u2192            api_key=self.api_key.to_dict(),\n   186\u2192            timeout=self.timeout,\n   187\u2192            max_retries=self.max_retries,\n   188\u2192            tools=[tool.to_dict() for tool in self.tools] if self.tools else None,\n   189\u2192            tools_strict=self.tools_strict,\n   190\u2192        )\n   191\u2192\n   192\u2192    @classmethod\n   193\u2192    def from_dict(cls, data: Dict[str, Any]) -> \"OpenAIChatGenerator\":\n   194\u2192        \"\"\"\n   195\u2192        Deserialize this component from a dictionary.\n   196\u2192\n   197\u2192        :param data: The dictionary representation of this component.\n   198\u2192        :returns:\n   199\u2192            The deserialized component instance.\n   200\u2192        \"\"\"\n   201\u2192        deserialize_secrets_inplace(data[\"init_parameters\"], keys=[\"api_key\"])\n   202\u2192        deserialize_tools_inplace(data[\"init_parameters\"], key=\"tools\")\n   203\u2192        init_params = data.get(\"init_parameters\", {})\n   204\u2192        serialized_callback_handler = init_params.get(\"streaming_callback\")\n   205\u2192        if serialized_callback_handler:\n   206\u2192            data[\"init_parameters\"][\"streaming_callback\"] = deserialize_callable(serialized_callback_handler)\n   207\u2192        return default_from_dict(cls, data)\n   208\u2192\n   209\u2192    @component.output_types(replies=List[ChatMessage])\n   210\u2192    def run(\n   211\u2192        self,\n   212\u2192        messages: List[ChatMessage],\n   213\u2192        streaming_callback: Optional[StreamingCallbackT] = None,\n   214\u2192        generation_kwargs: Optional[Dict[str, Any]] = None,\n   215\u2192        *,\n   216\u2192        tools: Optional[List[Tool]] = None,\n   217\u2192        tools_strict: Optional[bool] = None,\n   218\u2192    ):\n   219\u2192        \"\"\"\n   220\u2192        Invokes chat completion based on the provided messages and generation parameters.\n   221\u2192\n   222\u2192        :param messages:\n   223\u2192            A list of ChatMessage instances representing the input messages.\n   224\u2192        :param streaming_callback:\n   225\u2192            A callback function that is called when a new token is received from the stream.\n   226\u2192        :param generation_kwargs:\n   227\u2192            Additional keyword arguments for text generation. These parameters will\n   228\u2192            override the parameters passed during component initialization.\n   229\u2192            For details on OpenAI API parameters, see [OpenAI documentation](https://platform.openai.com/docs/api-reference/chat/create).\n   230\u2192        :param tools:\n   231\u2192            A list of tools for which the model can prepare calls. If set, it will override the `tools` parameter set\n   232\u2192            during component initialization.\n   233\u2192        :param tools_strict:\n   234\u2192            Whether to enable strict schema adherence for tool calls. If set to `True`, the model will follow exactly\n   235\u2192            the schema provided in the `parameters` field of the tool definition, but this may increase latency.\n   236\u2192            If set, it will override the `tools_strict` parameter set during component initialization.\n   237\u2192\n   238\u2192        :returns:\n   239\u2192            A dictionary with the following key:\n   240\u2192            - `replies`: A list containing the generated responses as ChatMessage instances.\n   241\u2192        \"\"\"\n   242\u2192        if len(messages) == 0:\n   243\u2192            return {\"replies\": []}\n   244\u2192\n   245\u2192        streaming_callback = streaming_callback or self.streaming_callback\n   246\u2192\n   247\u2192        api_args = self._prepare_api_call(\n   248\u2192            messages=messages,\n   249\u2192            streaming_callback=streaming_callback,\n   250\u2192            generation_kwargs=generation_kwargs,\n   251\u2192            tools=tools,\n   252\u2192            tools_strict=tools_strict,\n   253\u2192        )\n   254\u2192        chat_completion: Union[Stream[ChatCompletionChunk], ChatCompletion] = self.client.chat.completions.create(\n   255\u2192            **api_args\n   256\u2192        )\n   257\u2192\n   258\u2192        is_streaming = isinstance(chat_completion, Stream)\n   259\u2192        assert is_streaming or streaming_callback is None\n   260\u2192\n   261\u2192        if is_streaming:\n   262\u2192            completions = self._handle_stream_response(\n   263\u2192                chat_completion,  # type: ignore\n   264\u2192                streaming_callback,  # type: ignore\n   265\u2192            )\n   266\u2192        else:\n   267\u2192            assert isinstance(chat_completion, ChatCompletion), \"Unexpected response type for non-streaming request.\"\n   268\u2192            completions = [\n   269\u2192                self._convert_chat_completion_to_chat_message(chat_completion, choice)\n   270\u2192                for choice in chat_completion.choices\n   271\u2192            ]\n   272\u2192\n   273\u2192        # before returning, do post-processing of the completions\n   274\u2192        for message in completions:\n   275\u2192            self._check_finish_reason(message.meta)\n   276\u2192\n   277\u2192        return {\"replies\": completions}\n   278\u2192\n   279\u2192    @component.output_types(replies=List[ChatMessage])\n   280\u2192    async def run_async(\n   281\u2192        self,\n   282\u2192        messages: List[ChatMessage],\n   283\u2192        streaming_callback: Optional[StreamingCallbackT] = None,\n   284\u2192        generation_kwargs: Optional[Dict[str, Any]] = None,\n   285\u2192        *,\n   286\u2192        tools: Optional[List[Tool]] = None,\n   287\u2192        tools_strict: Optional[bool] = None,\n   288\u2192    ):\n   289\u2192        \"\"\"\n   290\u2192        Asynchronously invokes chat completion based on the provided messages and generation parameters.\n   291\u2192\n   292\u2192        This is the asynchronous version of the `run` method. It has the same parameters and return values\n   293\u2192        but can be used with `await` in async code.\n   294\u2192\n   295\u2192        :param messages:\n   296\u2192            A list of ChatMessage instances representing the input messages.\n   297\u2192        :param streaming_callback:\n   298\u2192            A callback function that is called when a new token is received from the stream.\n   299\u2192            Must be a coroutine.\n   300\u2192        :param generation_kwargs:\n   301\u2192            Additional keyword arguments for text generation. These parameters will\n   302\u2192            override the parameters passed during component initialization.\n   303\u2192            For details on OpenAI API parameters, see [OpenAI documentation](https://platform.openai.com/docs/api-reference/chat/create).\n   304\u2192        :param tools:\n   305\u2192            A list of tools for which the model can prepare calls. If set, it will override the `tools` parameter set\n   306\u2192            during component initialization.\n   307\u2192        :param tools_strict:\n   308\u2192            Whether to enable strict schema adherence for tool calls. If set to `True`, the model will follow exactly\n   309\u2192            the schema provided in the `parameters` field of the tool definition, but this may increase latency.\n   310\u2192            If set, it will override the `tools_strict` parameter set during component initialization.\n   311\u2192\n   312\u2192        :returns:\n   313\u2192            A dictionary with the following key:\n   314\u2192            - `replies`: A list containing the generated responses as ChatMessage instances.\n   315\u2192        \"\"\"\n   316\u2192        # validate and select the streaming callback\n   317\u2192        streaming_callback = select_streaming_callback(self.streaming_callback, streaming_callback, requires_async=True)  # type: ignore\n   318\u2192\n   319\u2192        if len(messages) == 0:\n   320\u2192            return {\"replies\": []}\n   321\u2192\n   322\u2192        api_args = self._prepare_api_call(\n   323\u2192            messages=messages,\n   324\u2192            streaming_callback=streaming_callback,\n   325\u2192            generation_kwargs=generation_kwargs,\n   326\u2192            tools=tools,\n   327\u2192            tools_strict=tools_strict,\n   328\u2192        )\n   329\u2192\n   330\u2192        chat_completion: Union[\n   331\u2192            AsyncStream[ChatCompletionChunk], ChatCompletion\n   332\u2192        ] = await self.async_client.chat.completions.create(**api_args)\n   333\u2192\n   334\u2192        is_streaming = isinstance(chat_completion, AsyncStream)\n   335\u2192        assert is_streaming or streaming_callback is None\n   336\u2192\n   337\u2192        if is_streaming:\n   338\u2192            completions = await self._handle_async_stream_response(\n   339\u2192                chat_completion,  # type: ignore\n   340\u2192                streaming_callback,  # type: ignore\n   341\u2192            )\n   342\u2192        else:\n   343\u2192            assert isinstance(chat_completion, ChatCompletion), \"Unexpected response type for non-streaming request.\"\n   344\u2192            completions = [\n   345\u2192                self._convert_chat_completion_to_chat_message(chat_completion, choice)\n   346\u2192                for choice in chat_completion.choices\n   347\u2192            ]\n   348\u2192\n   349\u2192        # before returning, do post-processing of the completions\n   350\u2192        for message in completions:\n   351\u2192            self._check_finish_reason(message.meta)\n   352\u2192\n   353\u2192        return {\"replies\": completions}\n   354\u2192\n   355\u2192    def _prepare_api_call(  # noqa: PLR0913\n   356\u2192        self,\n   357\u2192        *,\n   358\u2192        messages: List[ChatMessage],\n   359\u2192        streaming_callback: Optional[StreamingCallbackT] = None,\n   360\u2192        generation_kwargs: Optional[Dict[str, Any]] = None,\n   361\u2192        tools: Optional[List[Tool]] = None,\n   362\u2192        tools_strict: Optional[bool] = None,\n   363\u2192    ) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n   364\u2192        # update generation kwargs by merging with the generation kwargs passed to the run method\n   365\u2192        generation_kwargs = {**self.generation_kwargs, **(generation_kwargs or {})}\n   366\u2192\n   367\u2192        # adapt ChatMessage(s) to the format expected by the OpenAI API\n   368\u2192        openai_formatted_messages = [message.to_openai_dict_format() for message in messages]\n   369\u2192\n   370\u2192        tools = tools or self.tools\n   371\u2192        tools_strict = tools_strict if tools_strict is not None else self.tools_strict\n   372\u2192        _check_duplicate_tool_names(tools)\n   373\u2192\n   374\u2192        openai_tools = {}\n   375\u2192        if tools:\n   376\u2192            tool_definitions = []\n   377\u2192            for t in tools:\n   378\u2192                function_spec = {**t.tool_spec}\n   379\u2192                if tools_strict:\n   380\u2192                    function_spec[\"strict\"] = True\n   381\u2192                    function_spec[\"parameters\"][\"additionalProperties\"] = False\n   382\u2192                tool_definitions.append({\"type\": \"function\", \"function\": function_spec})\n   383\u2192            openai_tools = {\"tools\": tool_definitions}\n   384\u2192\n   385\u2192        is_streaming = streaming_callback is not None\n   386\u2192        num_responses = generation_kwargs.pop(\"n\", 1)\n   387\u2192        if is_streaming and num_responses > 1:\n   388\u2192            raise ValueError(\"Cannot stream multiple responses, please set n=1.\")\n   389\u2192\n   390\u2192        return {\n   391\u2192            \"model\": self.model,\n   392\u2192            \"messages\": openai_formatted_messages,  # type: ignore[arg-type] # openai expects list of specific message types\n   393\u2192            \"stream\": streaming_callback is not None,\n   394\u2192            \"n\": num_responses,\n   395\u2192            **openai_tools,\n   396\u2192            **generation_kwargs,\n   397\u2192        }\n   398\u2192\n   399\u2192    def _handle_stream_response(self, chat_completion: Stream, callback: SyncStreamingCallbackT) -> List[ChatMessage]:\n   400\u2192        chunks: List[StreamingChunk] = []\n   401\u2192        chunk = None\n   402\u2192\n   403\u2192        for chunk in chat_completion:  # pylint: disable=not-an-iterable\n   404\u2192            assert len(chunk.choices) == 1, \"Streaming responses should have only one choice.\"\n   405\u2192            chunk_delta: StreamingChunk = self._convert_chat_completion_chunk_to_streaming_chunk(chunk)\n   406\u2192            chunks.append(chunk_delta)\n   407\u2192\n   408\u2192            callback(chunk_delta)\n   409\u2192\n   410\u2192        return [self._convert_streaming_chunks_to_chat_message(chunk, chunks)]\n   411\u2192\n   412\u2192    async def _handle_async_stream_response(\n   413\u2192        self, chat_completion: AsyncStream, callback: AsyncStreamingCallbackT\n   414\u2192    ) -> List[ChatMessage]:\n   415\u2192        chunks: List[StreamingChunk] = []\n   416\u2192        chunk = None\n   417\u2192\n   418\u2192        async for chunk in chat_completion:  # pylint: disable=not-an-iterable\n   419\u2192            assert len(chunk.choices) == 1, \"Streaming responses should have only one choice.\"\n   420\u2192            chunk_delta: StreamingChunk = self._convert_chat_completion_chunk_to_streaming_chunk(chunk)\n   421\u2192            chunks.append(chunk_delta)\n   422\u2192\n   423\u2192            await callback(chunk_delta)\n   424\u2192\n   425\u2192        return [self._convert_streaming_chunks_to_chat_message(chunk, chunks)]\n   426\u2192\n   427\u2192    def _check_finish_reason(self, meta: Dict[str, Any]) -> None:\n   428\u2192        if meta[\"finish_reason\"] == \"length\":\n   429\u2192            logger.warning(\n   430\u2192                \"The completion for index {index} has been truncated before reaching a natural stopping point. \"\n   431\u2192                \"Increase the max_tokens parameter to allow for longer completions.\",\n   432\u2192                index=meta[\"index\"],\n   433\u2192                finish_reason=meta[\"finish_reason\"],\n   434\u2192            )\n   435\u2192        if meta[\"finish_reason\"] == \"content_filter\":\n   436\u2192            logger.warning(\n   437\u2192                \"The completion for index {index} has been truncated due to the content filter.\",\n   438\u2192                index=meta[\"index\"],\n   439\u2192                finish_reason=meta[\"finish_reason\"],\n   440\u2192        